@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include _uml-style.puml
title Cancellation during selection — UML sequence
hide footbox
participant "caller" as Caller
participant "<color:#FFFFFF>native front" as Front #1E4F78
participant "<color:#FFFFFF>policy worker" as Worker #1E4F78

Caller -> Front : start-session
create Worker
Front -> Worker : Start worker; check identity; send request
note over Front, Worker
  The worker evaluates trusted owner policy.
  It has no session-result context.
end note
== Cancellation reaches the front ==
Worker -> Front : SIGINT (the example below)
Front -> Worker : Close protocol; attempt bounded stop and wait
Front -> Front : Drain bounded diagnostics; attempt\nworker private-directory cleanup
note over Front, Worker
  Reap and removal must be confirmed before claiming them.
  Failed attempts remain diagnostics; no X certifies teardown here.
  No managed process is launched.
  No result channel is allocated.
end note
Front -> Front : Keep cancellation primary; retain any\noriginal failure and teardown problems
Front --> Caller : Report cancellation; re-raise INT\n(shell status 130); no result bytes

legend bottom
  Read downwards: order, not elapsed time. Dashed verticals: lifelines.
  Solid arrows: actions; dashed arrow: reported outcome; bent arrows: local work.
  Blue boxes: Ravel processes. Grey box: caller. Bars group related steps.
  This example sends INT directly to the front; it is not keyboard delivery.
  HUP and TERM give shell statuses 129 and 143 by the same cancellation rule.
  A failed signal propagation uses the corresponding numeric exit as fallback.
  Cancellation reports attempted teardown, not a guarantee that cleanup succeeded.
endlegend
@enduml
